          "question": "q-325169",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}={e}^{x}-3xy,\\,y(-2)=3\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $\u0394x=1.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and the current value $y.$",
