        {
          "question": "e-21312",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = 2x^2+3xy, \\qquad y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $\\Delta x = 1.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, $y_\\text{new},$ in terms of the new value $x_\\text{new}$ and the current value $y.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14046555/example-21312.json",
