    {
      "question": "e-21312",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "be966789d06d58ea6eda8b508c4ca92fcba4d51b5dccf84484b1d7927a460e87",
      "new_sha256": "0ad150302f8909d6a6873ae076bb96438963d179873e1cdef58e08df6240918b",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21312",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y_0 = y(x_0),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = y'_\\text{new} \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new},y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =(2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y$ and solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\u0394y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14046555/example-21312.json",
          "file_sha256": "1ced93ea9c12c67e99b6084201cf8461e0d3644d0f576e148ca33a59dd2ddc80"
        }
      ],
